            <div class="VideoLead-content"  data-orientation="landscape" >
                <bsp-read-more class="ReadMore" data-more-button-text="Read More" data-less-button-text="Read Less"
                    data-expand="ReadMore-expand" data-limit="110" data-main-class="ReadMore">
                    <div class="VideoLead-videoTitle"><p>The last time the District of Columbia had a freshman delegate going through new member orientation on Capitol Hill, the Soviet Union still existed, George H.W. Bush was president. Now Robert White Jr. is stepping into the role held by Eleanor Holmes Norton, a legendary advocate for Washington, D.C, who is retiring after 36 years. Speaking to The Associated Press, White said his priorities are the same — statehood for the city and improving the district’s economic situation. (AP Video by Nathan Ellgren)</p></div>
                </bsp-read-more>
                
            </div>
        
    
